          "description": "wakeup eof_reentry: a held client's EOF handled again; should stay 0. wakeup empty_out: woken to write with nothing to write; about one each time its answer queue fills and empties, growth with the time held is a busy loop. refused: would-be holds cut at their FIN because the next request was still arriving. accel skipped: connections left unaccelerated so that they could be held.",
